Protocol Buffers, Abseil, nghttp2 and opentelemetry-proto imports
=================================================================

contrib/protobuf, contrib/abseil-cpp, contrib/nghttp2 and
contrib/opentelemetry-proto are trimmed imports of upstream release
archives (versions and SHA256 in each contrib/*/README.5BSD and in
contrib/README.5BSD).  This directory holds what reproduces them.

trim.py SRC OUT
	Computes the keep sets from the pristine extracted archives in SRC
	(protobuf-29.6, abseil-cpp-20250127.1, nghttp2-1.70.0,
	opentelemetry-proto-1.10.0) and writes the trimmed trees and
	OUT/lists.json:
	  protobuf	the upstream CMake source lists (src/file_lists.cmake)
			for libprotobuf, libprotobuf-lite, libprotoc without the
			non-C++ generators, libupb, protoc-gen-upb,
			protoc-gen-upb_minitable and protoc-gen-upbdefs, the
			well-known and compiler .proto files, utf8_range, the
			version scripts, and every file reachable by #include
			"..." from those;
	  abseil-cpp	upstream's single-library composition
			(CMake/AbseilDll.cmake ABSL_INTERNAL_DLL_FILES) plus the
			include closure of it and of the kept protobuf files;
	  nghttp2	lib/ (the port's --enable-lib-only) and its includes;
	  opentelemetry-proto	the .proto files.
	License and notice files are always kept.  Tests, benchmarks,
	build systems of other platforms and the other language runtimes
	are not imported.

Install locations
	lib/protobuf/protobuf.dirs.mk: protoc in /usr/libexec (not on the
	default PATH; base components call it by its full path, and it must
	not shadow the ports protoc), the upb plugins in /usr/libexec.  The
	bootstrap copies use the same paths under ${WORLDTMP}/legacy.

patches/
	The local changes, applied to the trimmed trees with patch -p1 in
	the import directory:
	  abseil-a4950fba-is_trivially_relocatable.patch
		upstream commit a4950fba (the devel/abseil port applies the
		same commit): use __builtin_is_cpp_trivially_relocatable;
		clang 21 deprecates __is_trivially_relocatable.  The hunk for
		the omitted type_traits_test.cc is left out.
	  abseil-powerpc-timebase-frequency.patch
		the devel/abseil port's fix for the FreeBSD/powerpc
		kern.timecounter.tc.timebase.frequency sysctl width.
	  abseil-options-5bsd.patch
		absl/base/options.h for headers installed with a binary
		library: std::any/optional/string_view/variant always (C++17
		is required), absl::ordering always (the std alias needs
		C++20), and the inline namespace lts_20250127_5bsd, which
		differs from the ports' Abseil so the two never interpose.
	  protobuf-upb-defpool-oom.patch
		upb_DefPool_New() and _upb_DefPool_LoadDefInitEx() did not
		check upb_Arena_New(), so an allocation failure while loading
		compiled-in definitions crashed instead of failing (found by
		the libotelexport and libdtotel allocation-failure sweeps).
	  protobuf-default-proto-path.patch
		protoc also looks for the well-known types in
		<prefix>/include/private, where base installs them
		(/usr/libexec/../include/private).

genmk.py LISTS SRCTOP
	Rewrites the "# BEGIN generated" blocks (SRCS and INCSGROUPS) of
	lib/libabsl, lib/protobuf/*, libexec/protoc-gen-* and lib/libnghttp2
	Makefiles from OUT/lists.json, and prints the private include
	directories, which etc/mtree/BSD.usr.dist must list under
	usr/include/private.

Update procedure
	1. Fetch and verify the new archives against the 5BSD ports
	   distinfo (devel/protobuf, devel/abseil, www/libnghttp2,
	   devel/opentelemetry-proto) and review the ports' patches.
	2. Extract them, run trim.py, import the trimmed trees on the
	   vendor branches, merge, and reapply or drop patches/.
	3. Run genmk.py; update etc/mtree/BSD.usr.dist, SHLIB_MAJOR
	   (protobuf major, ABSL_SOVERSION, the nghttp2 libtool current
	   minus age), lib/libnghttp2/nghttp2/nghttp2ver.h and the inline
	   namespace in abseil-options-5bsd.patch.
	4. Update the Bazel targets (tools/build/bazel/targets) and rerun
	   the probe; rebuild the world and run the libotelexport tests.
